WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.399
Week 20: Preterite and Imperfect Together. tell a coherent story explain circumstances identify cause and interruption

2
00:00:08.399 --> 00:00:14.857
Cultural lens. Narrative stance in personal accounts, journalism, and oral histories.

3
00:00:14.857 --> 00:00:27.291
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:27.291 --> 00:00:39.299
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:39.299 --> 00:00:48.511
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:48.511 --> 00:01:18.609
Model language. Caminaba a casa cuando empezó la tormenta. — I was walking home when the storm began. Mientras todos dormían, sonó la alarma. — While everyone was sleeping, the alarm went off. Ya había poca luz cuando llegamos. — There was already little light when we arrived. De repente, un vecino abrió la puerta. — Suddenly, a neighbor opened the door. Al final resolvimos el problema juntos. — In the end, we solved the problem together.

7
00:01:18.609 --> 00:01:28.763
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
